{
  "title": "The Last Day of Zilhaj",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The last day of Zilhajj is the last day in the Arabic calendar. According to some narrations mentioned by Sayyid Ibn Taaoos in his book of Iqbal al-Aa’maal, it is recommended to offer a two unit prayer on this day reciting Surah al-Faatehah once, and repeating each of Surah al-Tawheed and Ayah al-Kursi ten times. After accomplishment, it is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَا عَمِلْتُ فِيْ هٰذِهِ السَّنَةِ \nALLAAHUMMA MAA AMILTO FEE HAAZEHIS SANATE \nO Allah, whatever deed I have committed in this year \nمِنْ عَمَلٍ نَهَيْتَنِيْ عَنْهُ \nMIN A’MALIN NAHAYTANEE A’NHO \nthat You forbade me from, \nوَ لَمْ تَرْضَهُ وَ نَسِيْتُهٗ وَ لَمْ تَنْسَهٗ \nWA LAM TARZAHO WA NASEETOHU WA LAM TANSAHU \nwhich You were not pleased with, and which I forgot but You did not forget, \nوَ دَعَوْتَنِيْ اِلَى التَّوْبَةِ بَعْدَ اجْتِرَاۤئِيْ عَلَيْكَ \nWA DA-A’WTANEE ELAT TAWBATE BA’DAJ TERAAA-EE A’LAYKA \nand You called me to repentance after my audacity against You—\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاِنِّيْ اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ مِنْهُ فَاغْفِرْ لِيْ \nALLAAHUMMA FA-INNEE ASTAGHFEROKA MINHO FAGHFIR LEE \nO Allah, I seek Your forgiveness for it, so forgive me. \nوَ مَا عَمِلْتُ مِنْ عَمَلٍ يُقَرِّبُنِيْ اِلَيْكَ فَاقْبَلْهُ مِنِّيْ \nWA MAA A’MILTO MIN A’MALIN YOQARREBONEE ELAYKA FAQBALHO MINNEE \nAnd whatever deed I have committed that brings me closer to You, accept it from me, \nوَ لَا تَقْطَعْ رَجَاۤئِيْ مِنْكَ يَا كَرِيْمُ.\nWA LAA TAQTA’ RAJAAA-EE MINKA YAA KAREEMO.\nand do not cut off my hope in You, O Generous One.\nIf these statements are said, Satan will say, “Woe to me! All the efforts that I have exerted throughout this year for misleading this person have been failed by the utterance of these statements.” Besides, one who says these words will be testified by the year that he sealed it in a good way."
}
